><given-names>D. E.</given-names><suffix>Jr.</suffix></name><name><surname>Kimelberg</surname><given-names>H. K.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>1994</year>). <article-title>The role of sulfhydryl groups in <sc>d</sc>-aspartate and rubidium release from neonatal rat primary astrocyte cultures</article-title>. <source>Brain Res.</source><volume>648</volume>, <fpage>16</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>23</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0006-8993(94)91899-6</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7922519</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B6"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bakken</surname><given-names>I. J.</given-names></name><name><surname>White</surname><given-names>L. R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Unsgard</surname><given-names>G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Aasly</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sonnewald</surname><given-names>U.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>1998</year>). <article-title>[U-<sup>13</sup>C]glutamate metabolism in astrocytes during hypoglycemia and hypoxia</article-title>. <source>J. Neurosci. Res.</source><volume>51</volume>, <fpage>636</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>645</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/(SICI)1097-4547(19980301)51:5&#x0003c;636::AID-JNR11&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-0</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9512008</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ballatori</surname><given-names>N.</given-names></name><name><surname>Krance</surname><given-names>S. M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Marchan</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Hammond</surname><given-names>C. L.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>2008</year>). <article-title>Plasma membrane glutathione transporters and their roles in cell physiology and pathophysiology</article-title>. <source>Mol. Aspects Med.</source> (in press).<pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.mam.2008.08.004</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18786560</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bi</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Jiang</surname><given-names>B.</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>J. H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lei</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>X. L.</given-names></name><name><surname>An</surname><given-names>L. J.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>2008</year>). <article-title>Protective effects of catalpol against H<sub>2</sub>O<sub>2</sub>-induced oxidative stress in astrocytes primary cultures</article-title>. <source>Neurosci. Lett.</source><volume>442</volume>, <fpage>224</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>227</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.neulet.2008.07.029</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18652878</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bickler</surname><given-names>P. E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kelleher</surname><given-names>J. A.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>1992</year>). <article-title>Fructose-1,6-bisphosphate stabilizes brain intracellular calcium during hypoxia in rats</article-title>. <source>Stroke</source><volume>23</volume>, <fpage>1617</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>1622</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1440710</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bishop</surname><given-names>G. M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Dringen</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Robinson</surname><given-names>S. R.</given-names></name></person-group> (<year>2007</year>). <article-title>Zinc stimulates the production of toxic rea